What is HTML?
# It is the Hypertext Markup language that is used to create and structure web pages.
# A basic HTML document has the following:- Structure tags- html, head, body and Content tags- h1, p, img, span, list.
# The .html extension specifies that a file contains HTML code and should be interpreted by a web browser as a web page.
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
    <head>
        <title>HTML Page</title>
        <body>
        </body>
    </head>
</html>

<meta charset="UTF-8"> This ensures that the characters are displayed correctly and without this some characters may appear as unknown symbols.
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"> This makes the width of the web page as the width of the device that is making it same responsive.

