SEMANTIC TAGS:-
# These are the tags that clearly describe the meaning and purpose of the content they contain.
# These improve readability, accessability and mainatinability of code.
<header> Tag
● Represents the header section of a webpage or specific sections.
● Typically contains site title, logo, and navigation.
<nav> Tag
● Used for navigation links. This should always be used when the links are to be added at the top sections and if needed at the lower sides of the web page, make use of the <a> tag.
. <main> Tag
● Marks the primary content of a webpage.
 <section> Tag
● Groups content into thematic sections, is used to group related content under a common topic. There will always be a heading tag at the start of each section to mention the theme of the section.
<article> Tag
● Represents a self-contained piece of content that can stand on its own and there should be a heading at the start of the article.
<aside> Tag
● Used for content related to the main content, like sidebars.
<footer> Tag
● Represents the footer section of a webpage.
<footer>
 <p>&copy; 2025 My Website. All rights reserved.</p>
</footer>

